Author: Iban Ameztoy | Joint Research Center - European Commission | DryForM Exploratory Research Project 2022-2024

version 1. Preliminary notes: The entire process can be further optimized. The outcomes still generate some artifacts mainly because some Sentinel-1 overlapping areas
                              These artifacts should be further fine tuned as to avoid inheritance in the classification process.
                              This is being developed under version 1.1. (not yet available as of May 2024)

This script processes Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 imagery for year 2020. It exports as an asset a cloud free stack of 72 bands, 18 per quarter:

    - MS bands 3, 4, 5, 8, 11 and 12
    - Different Indexes: MSAVI-2, gNDVI, BI and SI | Additional indexes are also added but not computed;
    - GLCM textures. Not all are calculated; only 7 indexes are calculated. The input for the GLCM is the "gray" band;
    - VH and VV polarizations from Sentinel-1 (Need to tackle artifacts, not included in this version);

    - Quarters are JAN-MAR, APR-JUN, JUL-SEP, OCT-DEC. This can be easily change to monthly, bimonthly,... composites. See t_int parameters;
    - Outcomes are casted to 8 bits to avoid storage capacity issues;

    - Target Year can be changed to any other year. If changed, parameters str, end, str0, end0 shall be also modified;
    
The processing is divided in tiles to avoid processing memory issues.
    - All the processing is included within a big function that runs over each tile;
    - Tiles are build upon FAO ecozones areas and using the covering grid method;
        - Scale parameter can be changed to get smaller or bigger tiles;
            - However, big tiles may throw a memory problem while small tiles generate a very big number of processing tasks;
        - The current parameter value (i.e. 100000 or 100x100 km tiles) was tested to optimize the process;
        - The tiles are further processed to adequate the IDs. This is necessary to get proper names while exporting;
        
        - This method can be further optimized (.evaluate). 
            - While running the current version, the browser may throw an error as the process is run on the client side;
            - If this happens, wait until the tasks are loaded in the Task tab;
            - The process will load as many tasks as tiles are available: It is recommended to install OEEex plugin - https://www.open-geocomputing.org/OEEex/
              - This allows to "Run all" processes at once.

** Sentinel-2         
Clouds and shadows are masked using CloudScore+. A threshold of 0.55 is used over the "cs" band. 
    - See documentation for more details: https://developers.google.com/earth-engine/datasets/catalog/GOOGLE_CLOUD_SCORE_PLUS_V1_S2_HARMONIZED
    - Sentinel-2 image collection is filtered beforehand:
      - Cloud presence is allowed: 65%. This parameter can be changed. 
      - The initial filtering dates go beyond target year (2020). This is to allow the interpolation step to find valid pixels outside the target year.
          - It should be taken into account that certain areas remain cloudy even if running the quarterly median reducer.
          
After masking clouds and shadows, a interpolation method is implemented per image. Based on: https://spatialthoughts.com/courses/google-earth-engine/
    -   Interpolation Formula: y = y1 + (y2-y1)*((t – t1) / (t2 – t1))

Once we get all the images interpolated, the following processes are implemented:
    - quarterly median composites for year 2020 (str, end), 
    - indexes
    - Gray band and GLCM textures
    
** Sentinel-1

    - Based on Mullissa A., Vollrath A., Braun, C., Slagter B., Balling J., Gou Y., Gorelick N.,  Reiche J. | Version: v1.2 | Date: 2021-04-01
          Different parameters can be modified depending on processing needs. See  "DEFINE SENTINEL-1 PARAMETERS" section.
          
If replicated, the user shall create an empty image collection where all tiles will be stored.


*/

